#9 [MEDIUM] Unchecked Deserialization: `config`
  at bench\programs\jito-restaking\vault_program\src\initialize_vault_ncn_ticket.rs:36 (InitializeVaultNcnTicket)
  confidence: Low

  `config` is deserialized with `try_from_slice_unchecked` in `InitializeVaultNcnTicket` while the account's owner is never verified (`owner_checked = false`) and its data's discriminator is never validated. Any account owned by any program can be passed here, so `try_from_slice_unchecked` runs over attacker-controlled bytes and every later check operates on fabricated state. Exploit: supply an account owned by a malicious program with a forged layout; the program deserializes it as its own state and writes derived data, which the attacker influenced.

  Suggestion:
  Verify the owner before deserializing: `if config.owner != program_id { return Err(ProgramError::IllegalOwner); }`, and validate the discriminator: `if data[0..8] != DISCRIMINATOR { return Err(ProgramError::InvalidAccountData); }`.

  Manual verification:
